# Faiz Muhammad Zubair | Data Analytics Portfolio

I use Python, SQL, and Streamlit to explore customer, sales, retention, and marketing questions through interactive dashboards.

> **Demo data:** These apps use simulated example data. The metrics and findings demonstrate the analyses and are not results from real companies.

## Live dashboards

| Project | Focus | Live app |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SaaS retention and churn | Retention cohorts, churn patterns, and at-risk users | [Open dashboard](https://faiz-saas-retention.streamlit.app/) |
| Sales and inventory | Sales trends, stock levels, and low-stock risk | [Open dashboard](https://faiz-sales-inventory.streamlit.app/) |
| Retail profitability | Profit and margin comparisons across products and regions | [Open dashboard](https://faiz-sales-profitability.streamlit.app/) |
| Customer segmentation (RFM) | Recency, frequency, monetary scoring, and segments | [Open dashboard](https://data-analyst-proto-folio-1.streamlit.app/) |
| Marketing campaign ROI | Spend, revenue, conversion, CAC, and ROI by channel | [Open dashboard](https://faiz-marketing-roi.streamlit.app/) |

## About

I am a data analytics graduate based in Pakistan. I enjoy turning business questions into clear analysis and practical dashboards, with a focus on customer behavior and commercial performance.

**Tools and methods:** Python, Pandas, NumPy, SQL, Streamlit, data visualization, cohort analysis, RFM segmentation, CAC, ROI, and business KPI reporting.

## Project details

### SaaS retention and churn
Explores monthly retention cohorts, churn patterns, and an inactivity-based at-risk rule. Includes an interactive Streamlit dashboard and analysis notebook.

### Sales and inventory
Brings sales and stock information together to review trends, product movement, and low-stock risk.

### Retail profitability
Uses SQL and Python to compare sales, profit, and margins by region, category, and discount level.

### Customer segmentation (RFM)
Scores customers by recency, frequency, and monetary value, then summarizes the resulting segments.

### Marketing campaign ROI
Compares campaign spend, conversions, revenue, customer acquisition cost, and return on investment across channels.

## Run a dashboard locally

For example, to run the SaaS dashboard:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/faizmuhammadzubair5-dot/Data-analyst-proto-folio.git
cd Data-analyst-proto-folio/saas_retention_portfolio
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

Each project folder includes its own `requirements.txt` and Streamlit entrypoint.

